  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **The Goin' Gets Tough from the Getgo** (1 other source): The tape required a flip immediately following the performance of this specific track [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Bumblebee**: rare: 10 archived performances [2]\n- **Shalom Absalom**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **Reggae Junky Jew**: rare: 4 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ajc03683_ween_1992-03-07** (recommended): source not stated; 16 songs; 55 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Ween opened for Uncle Tupelo, a show Jeff cites in his memoir as highly punk [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ajc03683_ween_1992-03-07**: taped by Aadam Jacobs; source: Realistic PZM Mics > Sony TC-D5M > Cassette (M) [1]. Also: Captured via Realistic PZM mics into Sony TC-D5M cassette, later transferred to Tascam DR-05 [1]",
